From: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
Subject: yaffs_glue: honour SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH

yaffsfs_CurrentTime() returns the wall clock, and Yaffs writes that value
to the access, modification and change time of every object header. An
image written twice from the same input therefore differs.

Read SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH and use it when it is set, as described in
https://reproducible-builds.org/specs/source-date-epoch/. Exit with an
error when the value is not a number, so a wrong value cannot pass as a
reproducible build.

Signed-off-by: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
---
 src/yaffs_glue.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/yaffs_glue.c
+++ b/src/yaffs_glue.c
@@ -27,7 +27,21 @@ void yaffsfs_Unlock(void) {
 }

 u32 yaffsfs_CurrentTime(void) {
-	return time(NULL);
+	const char *source_date_epoch = getenv("SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH");
+	unsigned long long epoch;
+	char *end;
+
+	if (!source_date_epoch || !*source_date_epoch) {
+		return time(NULL);
+	}
+
+	epoch = strtoull(source_date_epoch, &end, 10);
+	if (*end) {
+		fprintf(stderr, "SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH is not a number\n");
+		exit(1);
+	}
+
+	return epoch;
 }

 void yaffsfs_SetError(int err) {
